{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Kaṇhadinna","html":"<article id='thag2.30'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 2.30 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 2.30 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dukanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Twos </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Tatiyavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Three </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Kaṇhadinnattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Kaṇhadinna </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Upāsitā sappurisā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I regularly sat close by true persons </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sutā dhammā abhiṇhaso; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and learnt the teaching. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sutvāna paṭipajjissaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>What I learned, I practiced, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>añjasaṁ amatogadhaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the direct route whose objective is freedom from death. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Bhavarāgahatassa me sato, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I’ve slain the desire for continued existence, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Bhavarāgo puna me na vijjati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>it won’t be found in me again. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na cāhu na ca me bhavissati, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>It was not, and it won’t be in me, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na ca me etarahi vijjatī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and it isn’t found in me now. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Kaṇhadinno thero … </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>vaggo tatiyo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='uddana-intro'><span class='root'>Tassuddānaṁ </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<blockquote class='uddanagatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Uttaro bhaddajitthero, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sobhito valliyo isi; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vītasoko ca yo thero, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>puṇṇamāso ca nandako; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Bharato bhāradvājo ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kaṇhadinno mahāmunīti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span></p></blockquote></article>"}
